## 🚀 How to Set Up the Project  

### **1️⃣ Install Git & ns-3 Dependencies**  
Run the following command to install the required dependencies:  
```bash
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y git gcc g++ cmake python3 python3-venv
2️⃣ Clone This Repository

cd ~/Documents/workshop
git clone https://github.com/atharvakanchan25/ns3-5G-vs-WiFi-Simulation.git
cd ns3-5G-vs-WiFi-Simulation
3️⃣ Set Up a Virtual Environment (Optional for Python Users)
If you plan to analyze results using Python, create a virtual environment:


python3 -m venv ns3
source ns3/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
4️⃣ Install and Build ns-3
Since ns-3 is required for simulation, install it:


cd ~/Documents/workshop
git clone https://gitlab.com/nsnam/ns-3-dev.git ns-3
cd ns-3
mkdir build
cd build
cmake ..
cmake --build .

5️⃣ Copy the Simulation File to ns-3

cp ~/Documents/workshop/ns3-5G-vs-WiFi-Simulation/network_comparison.cc ~/Documents/workshop/ns-3/scratch/
6️⃣ Run the Simulation


cd ~/Documents/workshop/ns-3
./ns3 build
./ns3 run scratch/network_comparison | tee ~/Documents/workshop/ns3-5G-vs-WiFi-Simulation/output.txt

✅ This generates network performance data comparing 5G vs. Wi-Fi.

